************ INGRESS *************** 

Ingress is used to expose applications running inside AKS to external users.

Without Ingress:

Each service needs its own LoadBalancer and public IP.

With Ingress:

Multiple services can share a single public IP.
Ingress routes requests to the correct service based on URL path or hostname.

_________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
$$$$$$$$$ Steps for integrating our AKS with ingress controller END TO END $$$$$$$$$$$$$


1 Create a dedicated public IP and namespace for ingress controller .
2 Install ingress controller using helm (replace the pip of ingress controller which we created in step 01)
3 Deploy application and expose it using a ClusterIP service.
4 Create an Ingress resource with routing rules.
5 Point DNS to the Ingress public IP.
6 External traffic flows through NGINX Ingress → Service → Pod.











